homelab-search (0.2.42) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A tag path that is an ancestor of another on the same photo is no
    longer printed. One shot of Arches arrived carrying Utah, Utah|Moab
    and Utah|Moab|Arches National Park and printed all three, which read
    as one chain stuttering its way across the row.
  * This is the photo's own data, not an indexing fault: digiKam writes
    the whole chain as separate entries, and 456 of the 5,389 tagged
    photos here are like that. Dropping the short ones loses nothing now
    that every segment is its own link - "Utah" is still right there,
    clickable, inside the long path.
  * STRICT PREFIX ONLY, at a segment boundary. A branch that diverges is a
    different place and keeps its own line, so Utah|Moab|Arches alongside
    Landscape Arch|West Side|Bottom stays two entries. The trailing '|' in
    the test is the whole correctness of it: without it, Utah would also
    swallow a sibling tag named "Utah Valley".
  * Surviving branches get one line each. The old run-on used a middot
    between paths and a chevron between segments, and at this size those
    are the same squiggle - which is most of why the repetition was hard
    to read. Seven tagged photos in eight now show a single line; 582
    show two.
  * 0.2.41 went to the apt repo carrying a placeholder changelog - a
    scripting slip on my side - and reprepro will not replace a published
    version with different content, so it is superseded by this and
    reached no node.

