homelab-search (0.2.39) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The metadata chip is "Dimensions", not "Size" - the byte size is
    already on the headline a line above, and two chips called Size on one
    row is a question the reader has to stop and answer.
  * The FILE NAME is the link now, and "Open" is gone. Where the name goes
    still follows `viewable`, the same function the server uses to decide
    what it will serve inline, so a download-only type - html, svg, where
    serving inline from this origin would be stored XSS against the search
    session - gets a name that downloads rather than one that opens. The AI
    result list on the same page already worked this way, so the keyword
    list was the inconsistent half.
  * "Download" moved to immediately left of the name, quieter and smaller,
    with padding for a tap target since two links now share that line. The
    actions row is reduced to the caveats ("download only", "in trash") and
    is skipped entirely when there are none, instead of leaving an empty
    div under every result.
  * EVERY SEGMENT OF A TAG PATH IS A FILTER, not just the leaf. Clicking
    "Arizona" under a photo searches that node and everything filed below
    it - 1,428 photos where the leaf "Sedona" gives 656. The hierarchy is
    the whole value of these tags: the flat Keywords field already holds
    the leaf, so Sedona was findable and Arizona was not, even though its
    owner filed it there.
  * The `tag` filter has existed in the query layer since the tag tables
    landed with nothing able to ask for it - the same gap `person` had, and
    found the same way: by wiring up the thing that displays it. _filters
    now parses it, it counts toward whether the panel opens, and it has a
    visible "Photo tag" control in Files-only, so a tag arriving from a
    click is something you can see, edit and clear.
  * One filter_href helper for both the people and the tag links, rather
    than a second copy of the same two lines.
  * The closed-panel summary says "person: Dana" instead of "to/from Dana",
    which stopped being true when that box also started matching the faces
    tagged in a photo, and it names an active tag filter too.

