homelab-search (0.2.38) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Dates lose the seconds: "2026-09-19 02:24", not "...02:24:46". Nobody
    scans a result list to the second.
  * Done in the short_date helper rather than at the one chip where it was
    noticed, because a photo shows the same instant twice - the EXIF
    taken-at becomes the file's content_created_at, so it is both the
    headline date and the "Taken" chip. Trimming one would have rendered
    one timestamp two different ways on one line.
  * FIXED ON THE WAY: short_date('2026-09-19') returned '2026-09'. The
    timezone-offset pattern was unanchored, so on a date with no time it
    matched the '-19' and took the day with it. The offset is now only
    stripped after an actual time, and a trailing Z is handled too. Every
    column feeding this is timestamptz so Postgres always sends a time and
    it never surfaced - but one of these values is parsed out of a
    stranger's EXIF. Checked against twelve timestamp shapes.

